<ProjectLayout slug="opposable-thumb">
  <p>
  Hands held tools,<br />
  and tools made other tools.<br />
  We shaped stone, learned to control fire, built machines,<br />
  and eventually began to create something that could think for us.
</p>

<p>
  Technology always seems to carry us forward.<br />
  Faster, farther, more precisely.<br />
  But what does it mean to move forward,<br />
  and where are we going?
</p>

<p>
  We did not get here alone.
</p>

<p>
  What we made was always<br />
  passed on to others, transformed, and made again.<br />
  Perhaps the development of civilization depended less<br />
  on any single remarkable ability<br />
  than on the ways our thoughts continued through one another.
</p>

<p>
  Now machines learn, create, and respond.<br />
  As they begin to resemble us more and more,<br />
  perhaps we, too, are slowly beginning to resemble them.
</p>

<p>
  Maybe what matters is not<br />
  how far we are able to go,<br />
  but what we carry with us along the way.
</p>

<p>
  And who we go with.
</p>

